# Code owners.
#
# Solo project today, so a single catch-all. The commented rules below are the
# intended split when a second person joins — they double as documentation of
# which areas need which expertise.
#
# > IMPORTANT: leave branch protection's "Require review from Code Owners"
# > OFF while this is a single-owner file. GitHub does not let you approve your
# > own PR, so requiring code-owner review on a solo repo blocks every merge.
# > Turn it on in the same change that adds a second owner.

* @jorge

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Future per-path ownership (uncomment as the team grows)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Frontend — UI, routing, accessibility
# /app/                       @frontend-owner
# /components/                @frontend-owner

# Money math. The product IS this code; review it like it can lose someone's
# savings, because a bug here does exactly that.
# /lib/core/                  @backend-owner @owner

# Schema and data isolation. A wrong RLS policy is a data breach.
# /supabase/                  @backend-owner @owner
# /supabase/tests/rls/        @backend-owner @owner

# Server-side data access and Server Actions — the authorization boundary.
# /lib/server/                @backend-owner

# CI has repository write potential; a compromised workflow is a supply-chain
# problem, not a build problem.
# /.github/workflows/         @devops-owner @owner
# /.github/actions/           @devops-owner @owner

# Architecture decisions outlive the people who make them.
# /docs/architecture/         @owner
# /docs/adr/                  @owner
# /docs/security/             @owner @security-reviewer

# Process changes affect everyone, so everyone should see them.
# /workflow/                  @owner
